setLogger(LSPServer,Function) -- set up logging for an LSP server
*****************************************************************

  * Function: setLogger (missing documentation)
  * Usage: 
        setLogger(server, f)
  * Inputs:
      * server, a *note LSP server: LSPServer,, 
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, 

Description
===========

Sets a custom logging function for server.  The function f should accept a
single string.  For example, to log to standard error:

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : server = new LSPServer     |
|                                |
|o1 = server                     |
|                                |
|o1 : LSPServer                  |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : setLogger(server, printerr)|
|                                |
|o2 = printerr                   |
|                                |
|o2 : FunctionClosure            |
+--------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note setLogger(LSPServer,Function): setLogger_lpLSPServer_cmFunction_rp,
    -- set up logging for an LSP server
